    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-056: CSS `background:` URL forms (image + repeat + position + size)**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~280 lines across 3 commits) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\nCloses the last 4 of 11 Wikipedia forms. **Reaches 100% form coverage for the first time since ADR-045.**\n\n## The measurement that shaped this ADR\n\nBlock backgrounds have **zero** url-form infrastructure today:\n\n| Layer | Block bg | Inline bg (ADR-045) | Mask (ADR-047) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fields for size/pos | ❌ | ✅ `bg_size_w/h`, `bg_pos_x/y` | ✅ `mask_size_w/h`, `mask_pos_x/y` |\n| Fields for repeat | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ `mask_no_repeat` (declared, unused) |\n| Cairo pattern matrix | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Paint honors position | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Paint honors size | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |\n\n**The full pattern exists twice already.** Just not in block backgrounds.\n\n## Scope (Shape A — full, 3 commits)\n\n### Commit 1: Infrastructure (no behavior change)\n\n- **`LayoutBox` + 5 fields** mirroring mask: `background_size_w/h`, `background_pos_x/y`, `background_no_repeat`\n- **`layout_element` reads** `background-size`, `background-position`, `background-repeat` (mirror mask's block at layout.cpp:558)\n- **`paint_image` splits**: `paint_img_element` (existing stretch for `<img>`) + `paint_background_image` (new size/pos/repeat honoring)\n- **At this commit:** `try_expand_background` still drops `url()` — no behavior change from ADR-055\n\n### Commit 2: Grammar parser (the visible delta)\n\nReplace 3 early-return lines with full CSS shorthand grammar:\n```\nbackground: [color || image || repeat || position [/ size]]*\n```\n\nOrder-free per spec. Each token classified independently.\n\n**This is where the visible delta lands.** After this commit, Wikipedia icons render.\n\n### Commit 3: Fixture + docs\n\n5-row permanent fixture, screenshot verification, Post-ADR-056 notes in 045/047/055.\n\n## The regression concern (flagged in spec)\n\n**`paint_image` serves both block backgrounds AND `<img>` elements today.** The new size/pos/repeat fields are block-background-only. Commit 1 must split into two functions to avoid regressing `<img>` rendering.\n\nVerified via existing ADR-034 img tests — **all must still pass after Commit 1**.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**4 of 5 Wikipedia `background:` URL forms render correctly** after ADR-056:\n\n| Form | Renders |\n|---|---|\n| `#fff url(checker) repeat` | ✅ white + tiled checker |\n| `url(pdf-icon) no-repeat right` | ✅ PDF icon, right-aligned |\n| `url(arrow-down) 100% 50% no-repeat` | ✅ arrow, right/center |\n| `#fff url(...) repeat` (var) | ✅ white + tiled |\n| `no-repeat center / 1.23em url(search)` | ⚠ **renders, ~10px too high** |\n\nThe 5th (search magnifier) has the correct size, but the element sits at `y=7` (container top) and needs `translateY(-50%)` to center — **blocked on `parent_content_height`** (same blocker as ADR-053/054). After ADR-056 the icon renders; it's just 10px above where CSS would place it. Better than invisible.\n\n**11/11 `background:` forms parse.** From 7/11 pre-ADR-056.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- `translateY(-50%)` / `top: 50%` (blocked on `parent_content_height`)\n- Percentage `background-size` (needs element dims in parser)\n- `cover` / `contain` (needs paint-time aspect math)\n- `repeat-x` / `repeat-y` / `space` / `round` (variants)\n- Multi-layer backgrounds\n- `linear-gradient` / `radial-gradient`\n- `background-clip` / `background-origin`\n\n## Test count target\n\n- 658 → ~668 (+10 tests)\n- Zero regression on existing ADR-034 img tests\n\nRefs #248\n",
